In article <1992Nov14.031920.12162@informix.com> hartman@informix.com
(Robert Hartman) writes:

>So ... I have a magic marker and I get a blank scroll.  Now I want
>to write on it.  Any suggestions as to what I might want to write?

What you will be able to write is dependant on two things; what
scrolls you have already identified (use '\' to find that out), and
how many charges the magic marker has.  You won't be able to write a
scroll you haven't identified (Calling one works as well as id'ing
it).  Nor will you be able to write a scroll that drains the m.m. of
more charges than it has.  There is a table about somewhere listing
the charges that each scroll requires; costs range between 4-30
charges and are *not* totally fixed.  Also, a blessed magic marker
always writes blessed scrolls, unless the scroll of blank paper is
cursed, in which case the scroll created will be uncursed.

The first scroll I would write is a blessed scroll of charging, for
recharging the m.m. when it runs low on charges.  After that, it
really depends on what you have and what you need.  I like to identify
*everything*, so I usually write lots of blessed scrolls of identify.
If you have say a +0 helm of brilliance or +0 gloves of dexterity, you
might want to write a few scrolls of enchant armor.

